I try to repro and fix it, but because i dont understand the lua stuff it wasn't easy to write an acceptable functional test for it, even with ai assist, so i don't open a PR, but i do have a patch that seem work on my device. so i think i can share it here.

add a global var `initaldir` and store the directory at `main.c` and pass it in `src/nvim/ex_docmd.c:ex_restart`
```
Channel *channel = channel_job_start(argv, exepath,
                                       CALLBACK_READER_INIT, on_err, CALLBACK_NONE,
                                       false, true, true, detach, kChannelStdinPipe,
                                       initialdir, 0, 0, NULL, &exit_status);
```

To drop the `[files]` in `ex_restart()`
```
bool keep_next = false;  // Mark next arg as an option value, keep it.
  TV_LIST_ITER_CONST(l, li,{
...
// Long options that take a value
    if (i > 0
        && (strequal(arg, "--cmd")
            || strequal(arg, "--server")
            || strequal(arg, "--startuptime")
            || strequal(arg, "--listen"))) {
      argv[i++] = xstrdup(arg);
      keep_next = true;
      continue;
    }
    // Short options that take a value
    if (i > 0
        && (strequal(arg, "-u")
            || strequal(arg, "-c")
            || strequal(arg, "-S")
            || strequal(arg, "-i")
            || strequal(arg, "-t")
            || strequal(arg, "-q")
            || strequal(arg, "-w")
            || strequal(arg, "-W"))) {
      argv[i++] = xstrdup(arg);
      keep_next = true;
      continue;
    }
...
}
```

i also have a simple repro.lua that print the log, and the content in log seem ok to me

